  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward bias in true prices vs model during rally regimes: model persistently underestimates level by ~+2 to +10 EUR, with the gap generally widening with horizon (largest errors around days 10–25). Apply a regime uplift when last 10–20d trend is positive.",
    "Lag/underreaction to momentum: after a breakout (e.g., move from low-70s to 80+), the model tracks the move but stays several EUR below for ~2–3 weeks. Add a momentum term: if 5–10d return > threshold, shift the whole forecast path upward and steepen early-horizon slope.",
    "Peak/turning-point mis-timing: model often predicts a decline too early (forecasts roll over while true prices keep rising). Delay mean-reversion signals by ~5–10 trading days when trend strength is high.",
    "Downturn underestimation at the very end of horizon: when the true series finally corrects (late examples), the model remains too high and too smooth. Add late-horizon downside convexity: if prices have been elevated (e.g., >20d above MA), increase probability/magnitude of a pullback in days 20–30.",
    "Volatility compression: forecast paths are smoother than realized outcomes (misses amplitude of both rallies and pullbacks). Inflate forecast variance and allow larger step-changes following large daily moves (|Δ| > ~1.5–2 EUR)."
  ]
}
